1
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:06,006
[LICIA] Now, let us commence
the operation

2
00:00:06,089 --> 00:00:08,300
to rescue our Lord Ars
from this scum.

3
00:00:08,383 --> 00:00:09,843
Failure is not an option.

4
00:00:10,427 --> 00:00:13,096
We cannot let a single one
escape their punishment.

5
00:00:13,514 --> 00:00:15,432
So who will be
in charge of the mission?

6
00:00:15,515 --> 00:00:17,976
Rosell's in the middle of talks
down at the harbor.

7
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:20,229
And it would take near forever
to summon Mireille

8
00:00:20,312 --> 00:00:21,980
from all the way over
in Lamberg.

9
00:00:22,064 --> 00:00:23,649
[LICIA] Yes, you're right.

10
00:00:24,358 --> 00:00:25,943
So it's going to have to be me.

11
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:27,194
You know Lord Ars
wouldn't like that!

12
00:00:27,277 --> 00:00:28,237
Get a hold of yourself!

13
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:30,113
You had better unhand me
at once, Charlotte!

14
00:00:30,197 --> 00:00:31,615
I know you're mad,
but you can't fight them.

15
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:32,741
I'll tear them limb from limb...

16
00:00:33,075 --> 00:00:34,534
[THOMAS] Then perhaps
you'll allow me to handle

17
00:00:34,618 --> 00:00:36,453
-this operation for you?
-[ALL] Uh?

18
00:00:37,246 --> 00:00:38,413
[LICIA] Thomas?

19
00:00:40,499 --> 00:00:42,751
[♪ opening theme song playing]

20
00:02:11,256 --> 00:02:13,050
[LICIA] I'd heard Mireille
went to Arcantez

21
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:14,676
in hopes of recruiting you.

22
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:18,096
Does this mean
you've accepted her offer?

23
00:02:19,222 --> 00:02:20,682
I haven't decided

24
00:02:20,766 --> 00:02:23,018
whether to serve
in an official capacity,

25
00:02:23,101 --> 00:02:24,394
but I couldn't help
but overhear,

26
00:02:24,478 --> 00:02:25,896
and I'd be happy to...

27
00:02:25,979 --> 00:02:27,189
[gasps softly]

28
00:02:27,939 --> 00:02:30,734
[LICIA] Thomas, I'm eternally
grateful to you.

29
00:02:30,817 --> 00:02:32,652
I just told you, I'm not--

30
00:02:32,736 --> 00:02:35,322
I could never fully repay you
for your help,

31
00:02:35,405 --> 00:02:38,325
and to have a former enemy
assist us in such a way.

32
00:02:38,408 --> 00:02:39,618
[Thomas exhales]

33
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:40,869
I simply realized

34
00:02:40,952 --> 00:02:43,372
that I'd rather work
with Ars than Couran.

35
00:02:43,455 --> 00:02:46,541
But I will help you.
I will bring him home.

36
00:02:47,042 --> 00:02:48,043
Great!

37
00:02:48,585 --> 00:02:50,253
Join Braham and Zaht!

38
00:02:50,337 --> 00:02:52,172
I will pray
for your success here.

39
00:02:52,255 --> 00:02:54,424
Please bring back
Lord Ars safely!

40
00:02:54,508 --> 00:02:55,967
Yeah, it'll be a piece of cake.

41
00:02:56,051 --> 00:02:57,678
We'll have him back
before you know it.

42
00:02:58,261 --> 00:03:00,680
See that you do that.
Don't fail me.

43
00:03:00,764 --> 00:03:02,182
[both exclaim nervously]

44
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:06,228
[THOMAS] Tell me,
how do you suggest we proceed?

45
00:03:06,311 --> 00:03:07,896
I'm not too worried about it.

46
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:09,773
I mean, they're just bandits,
aren't they?

47
00:03:09,856 --> 00:03:11,733
The Canarre Army
kicks so much ass

48
00:03:11,817 --> 00:03:14,403
that we'll just go there
and stomp their heads in.

49
00:03:14,486 --> 00:03:15,570
And what makes you think

50
00:03:15,862 --> 00:03:18,115
that they'll even decide
to engage us in a fight?

51
00:03:18,198 --> 00:03:20,742
If we sent a lot of troops,
I imagine they'd flee.

52
00:03:20,826 --> 00:03:22,953
What would become
of the hostages then?

53
00:03:23,036 --> 00:03:26,331
Hmm. Yeah, they'd kill them
so they wouldn't slow them down.

54
00:03:26,415 --> 00:03:27,332
Guess you're right.

55
00:03:27,416 --> 00:03:28,792
Yes, I am.

56
00:03:28,875 --> 00:03:30,877
And then the lady of the house
would kill you.

57
00:03:30,961 --> 00:03:33,088
[Joe gasps]
She would, wouldn't she?

58
00:03:34,714 --> 00:03:37,134
[Licia chuckles menacingly]

59
00:03:37,592 --> 00:03:39,553
You just show up
and start calling the shots?

60
00:03:39,636 --> 00:03:41,179
Who the hell
do you think you are?

61
00:03:41,263 --> 00:03:42,305
Our elite battalion

62
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:44,433
is the best group of soldiers
there ever was.

63
00:03:44,516 --> 00:03:46,268
We can handle
these punks ourselves.

64
00:03:46,351 --> 00:03:48,812
-Listen, kid.
-Huh? Say what?

65
00:03:48,895 --> 00:03:51,773
[THOMAS] How could you be
as impressive as you claim

66
00:03:51,857 --> 00:03:54,025
if your only plan
is to just barge in

67
00:03:54,109 --> 00:03:56,653
and start swinging
your swords around?

68
00:03:56,737 --> 00:04:00,574
First, it's crucial
that you know your enemy.

69
00:04:00,657 --> 00:04:01,783
Huh?

70
00:04:03,618 --> 00:04:06,079
[JOE] This is where
those guys were ambushed.

71
00:04:06,163 --> 00:04:08,582
No real sign
of anyone around here, though.

72
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:12,836
[THOMAS] Hmm... Uh?

73
00:04:14,254 --> 00:04:15,714
They've been gone for a while.

74
00:04:16,715 --> 00:04:18,592
-Look at this.
-[BOTH] Huh?

75
00:04:19,217 --> 00:04:21,011
-[THOMAS] See anything?
-[JOE] Huh?

76
00:04:21,094 --> 00:04:23,680
Looks like a dead campfire
and an old bucket.

77
00:04:24,764 --> 00:04:28,018
The bucket's made of steel,
very strong.

78
00:04:28,101 --> 00:04:31,146
They mainly use wood
for these things in Missian,

79
00:04:31,229 --> 00:04:32,981
so you don't see
many metal buckets

80
00:04:33,064 --> 00:04:34,274
around these parts.

81
00:04:34,357 --> 00:04:36,693
And one made of steel
is a bit of a luxury.

82
00:04:36,776 --> 00:04:38,153
It's uncommon, at least.

83
00:04:38,236 --> 00:04:39,988
Oh, yeah. I suppose you're right
about that.

84
00:04:40,071 --> 00:04:41,406
If they knew

85
00:04:41,490 --> 00:04:43,533
that your soldiers were coming
to rout their camp,

86
00:04:43,617 --> 00:04:46,661
do you think they'd just leave
something like this behind?

87
00:04:47,078 --> 00:04:49,915
Well, maybe if they were
in a big hurry.

88
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:52,292
Where are you going with this,
anyway?

89
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:53,919
[Thomas sighs]

90
00:04:54,002 --> 00:04:55,879
What's the point
of even having a brain

91
00:04:55,962 --> 00:04:57,672
if you refuse to use it?

92
00:04:57,756 --> 00:04:59,883
You really need
some proper schooling.

93
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:01,551
-Hmm.
-You think so?

94
00:05:02,511 --> 00:05:03,720
-[THOMAS] Let's go.
-[JOE] What?

95
00:05:03,803 --> 00:05:05,639
Wait, hold on just a second.

96
00:05:07,015 --> 00:05:09,100
Hey, why do I need schooling?

97
00:05:09,601 --> 00:05:12,938
Do you know what the necessary
ingredients are to make steel?

98
00:05:13,021 --> 00:05:15,482
Huh? Um, let's see.

99
00:05:19,861 --> 00:05:20,779
Is that it?

100
00:05:21,279 --> 00:05:22,364
♪

101
00:05:24,825 --> 00:05:27,327
Hmm, I do see a few guards.

102
00:05:27,953 --> 00:05:30,580
An eagle eye, huh? Hmm.

103
00:05:31,164 --> 00:05:32,374
I see them.

104
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:34,543
You notice anything?

105
00:05:35,585 --> 00:05:38,380
They've got banged up
Seitz military uniforms

106
00:05:38,463 --> 00:05:39,464
and equipment.

107
00:05:39,548 --> 00:05:41,132
-Yeah.
-[THOMAS] I had a hunch

108
00:05:41,216 --> 00:05:43,426
based on what we found
at that abandoned campsite.

109
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:45,387
Now, why would these bandits

110
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:47,472
have all these
Seitz uniforms and gear?

111
00:05:47,556 --> 00:05:49,933
I bet it's because
they stole 'em.

112
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:52,561
So you think they went
to a neighboring province

113
00:05:52,644 --> 00:05:54,604
just to steal their uniforms?

114
00:05:54,688 --> 00:05:56,356
Sounds like
too much trouble to me.

115
00:05:56,439 --> 00:05:58,984
Hmm. Yeah, that's fair.

116
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:02,070
Seitz happens to be
a major steel producer,

117
00:06:02,153 --> 00:06:03,863
and it complements
the magistones

118
00:06:03,947 --> 00:06:05,448
that they can mine there.

119
00:06:05,532 --> 00:06:07,534
They make steel, do they?

120
00:06:07,617 --> 00:06:09,786
You said that bucket
back at the campsite

121
00:06:09,870 --> 00:06:11,454
was made of steel, didn't you?

122
00:06:11,538 --> 00:06:15,458
So, do you think that means
they're soldiers from Seitz?

123
00:06:15,542 --> 00:06:18,295
Like, that would explain
the uniforms and stuff, huh?

124
00:06:18,378 --> 00:06:19,588
[THOMAS] Indeed.

125
00:06:20,046 --> 00:06:22,799
Instead of rejoining the army
after the war, they went rogue.

126
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:24,259
It's not that uncommon.

127
00:06:24,342 --> 00:06:27,304
Wait, you mean I was right?
That's crazy.

128
00:06:27,387 --> 00:06:28,888
You managed
to figure all that out

129
00:06:28,972 --> 00:06:30,724
just by finding a random bucket
laying around?

130
00:06:30,807 --> 00:06:32,726
Of course I could.

131
00:06:32,809 --> 00:06:35,854
Our problem now
is if we try to rush in,

132
00:06:35,937 --> 00:06:38,273
they'll burn the place down
and run off.

133
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,567
Then we gotta figure out a way--

134
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:42,402
Yes, we're going to need
a solid plan

135
00:06:42,485 --> 00:06:44,029
to rescue Ars Louvent.

136
00:06:44,112 --> 00:06:47,490
Canarre could fall if we fail,
and that's on your shoulders.

137
00:06:48,325 --> 00:06:49,492
So use your head.

138
00:06:51,453 --> 00:06:52,746
Let me think.

139
00:06:53,788 --> 00:06:55,206
From what I've been hearing,

140
00:06:55,290 --> 00:06:57,876
there are more guys
joining these bandits every day.

141
00:06:57,959 --> 00:07:00,754
So where could all these
new recruits be coming from?

142
00:07:01,338 --> 00:07:02,464
They can't all be guys

143
00:07:02,756 --> 00:07:05,091
who quit the Seitz army
going over to Missian.

144
00:07:05,717 --> 00:07:08,887
No, they gotta be recruiting
other brigands.

145
00:07:10,138 --> 00:07:12,098
I've got an awesome idea.

146
00:07:12,182 --> 00:07:14,768
We can dress up as brigands
and ask to join them.

147
00:07:14,851 --> 00:07:17,812
With a bunch of new recruits,
a couple more won't stand out.

148
00:07:18,313 --> 00:07:21,358
You start using your head
and you'll get better results.

149
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:23,276
Remember that next time, kid.

150
00:07:24,027 --> 00:07:27,781
Whoa! Hell yeah!
I'm freaking amazing, aren't I?

151
00:07:27,864 --> 00:07:30,450
Keep it down, you idiot!
They're gonna hear you!

152
00:07:30,533 --> 00:07:31,534
[Zaht gasps softly]

153
00:07:31,993 --> 00:07:34,496
He actually got this dimwit
to think for once?

154
00:07:34,579 --> 00:07:35,955
Don't get ahead of yourself,
okay?

155
00:07:36,289 --> 00:07:39,084
[ZAHT] With a brilliant guy like
Thomas Grangeon on our side,

156
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:40,919
there's no telling
what we can do.

157
00:07:41,753 --> 00:07:44,464
Who should we choose
to infiltrate their group?

158
00:07:44,547 --> 00:07:46,466
Obviously, we need
someone who's clever.

159
00:07:46,549 --> 00:07:47,967
Yeah. That's me!

160
00:07:48,051 --> 00:07:50,303
[ZAHT] I don't think this is
a good fit for you, Captain.

161
00:07:50,387 --> 00:07:51,680
What do you mean by that?

162
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:55,225
[ZAHT] Honestly, I don't think
you really want that answer.

163
00:07:55,308 --> 00:07:56,685
Yeah, you're right.

164
00:07:56,768 --> 00:08:00,188
Well then,
I guess it'll have to be me.

165
00:08:00,271 --> 00:08:02,732
Right on! You got this, man!

166
00:08:02,816 --> 00:08:03,692
Shut up!

167
00:08:06,528 --> 00:08:08,863
-[BANDIT 1] Hmm?
-Who's that?

168
00:08:09,406 --> 00:08:14,619
[BANDIT 1] I don't know, but...

169
00:08:14,703 --> 00:08:16,079
he's alone.

170
00:08:18,581 --> 00:08:19,666
[BANDIT 2] Hey, man,

171
00:08:19,749 --> 00:08:22,001
did you mean
to walk up here, or what?

172
00:08:22,085 --> 00:08:25,922
Yeah. My name's Rubius
and I came over from Paradille.

173
00:08:26,005 --> 00:08:28,091
No way, you liar!

174
00:08:28,174 --> 00:08:29,926
You're a Missian soldier,
ain't you?

175
00:08:30,010 --> 00:08:31,344
You got some kinda death wish?

176
00:08:31,428 --> 00:08:33,179
Now, why in the hell
would you fellas think

177
00:08:33,263 --> 00:08:35,306
I'd be lying to you
about where I'm from?

178
00:08:35,390 --> 00:08:37,726
You know, I think this guy's
telling the truth

179
00:08:37,809 --> 00:08:40,311
because that accent definitely
sounds Paradillian to me.

180
00:08:40,395 --> 00:08:41,479
[chuckles]

181
00:08:41,563 --> 00:08:43,898
I came here hoping
to find some work.

182
00:08:43,982 --> 00:08:46,067
You think you got enough room
in your group for another?

183
00:08:46,151 --> 00:08:47,986
-Oh?
-[laughter]

184
00:08:48,069 --> 00:08:49,404
Sorry, but we're full.

185
00:08:49,487 --> 00:08:52,240
Definitely not taking
just any guy that walks up.

186
00:08:52,323 --> 00:08:54,576
So I suggest that you be
on your merry way.

187
00:08:55,326 --> 00:08:57,370
You can leave
that bag here, though.

188
00:08:57,454 --> 00:08:59,998
Oh, come on.
You may have enough numbers,

189
00:09:00,081 --> 00:09:02,459
but don't you want guys who know
how to handle themselves?

190
00:09:03,501 --> 00:09:05,336
Oh, yeah, of course.

191
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:07,714
My question is,
does that mean you?

192
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:11,176
Don't think so. [grunting]

193
00:09:11,259 --> 00:09:12,218
[gasps]

194
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:14,804
[groans]

195
00:09:14,888 --> 00:09:16,556
You guys need
to learn some manners.

196
00:09:17,098 --> 00:09:19,768
I got quite the reputation
back in Paradille.

197
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:22,145
Yeah, about 10 years ago,

198
00:09:22,228 --> 00:09:24,022
I was drinking buddies
with this guy,

199
00:09:24,105 --> 00:09:26,191
an old bandit boss
by the name of Georg.

200
00:09:26,858 --> 00:09:28,818
You're saying you know Georg?

201
00:09:28,902 --> 00:09:31,112
Funny you would say that.
I worked with him,

202
00:09:31,196 --> 00:09:32,989
and he never once mentioned
your name.

203
00:09:33,072 --> 00:09:34,699
And we were
old drinkin' buddies, too.

204
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:37,660
What a coincidence, though.

205
00:09:37,744 --> 00:09:40,830
He's inside the castle
right now. Wanna say hello?

206
00:09:41,498 --> 00:09:42,749
[smirks]

207
00:09:42,832 --> 00:09:45,293
Yeah, sure. Haven't had a drink

208
00:09:45,376 --> 00:09:46,836
with his old ass
in quite a while.

209
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:47,962
[both gasp]

210
00:09:48,379 --> 00:09:50,298
I think he really does know him.

211
00:09:50,381 --> 00:09:53,343
All right. We'll let you inside
to meet the boss man.

212
00:09:54,761 --> 00:09:56,387
Had to make sure you're legit.

213
00:09:56,471 --> 00:09:58,306
Lots of guys
come around dropping names

214
00:09:58,389 --> 00:10:00,100
to seem like big shots.

215
00:10:00,558 --> 00:10:01,601
[ZAHT] I'm sure.

216
00:10:03,853 --> 00:10:05,230
[BANDIT 3] The truth of it is,

217
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:07,440
Georg's been dead
for a while now.

218
00:10:07,524 --> 00:10:09,859
I was just
messing with you earlier.

219
00:10:09,943 --> 00:10:11,653
Well, ain't that a shame.

220
00:10:11,736 --> 00:10:13,780
I'll raise a glass
to his memory.

221
00:10:14,656 --> 00:10:15,865
I knew he was dead.

222
00:10:16,658 --> 00:10:17,700
I oughta,

223
00:10:18,201 --> 00:10:20,870
because I killed him myself
back in my mercenary days.

224
00:10:22,914 --> 00:10:26,417
The infiltration's a success.
Time to get to work.

225
00:10:27,544 --> 00:10:31,047
Braham, Thomas,
you gotta do your part.

226
00:10:46,479 --> 00:10:48,940
[ARS] Hey.
Can't sleep either, huh?

227
00:10:51,317 --> 00:10:54,612
I'm sorry to have dragged you
into this mess along with us.

228
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:57,407
I'm sure you must be nervous,

229
00:10:57,490 --> 00:10:59,534
but I'm positive
that help is on the way.

230
00:10:59,617 --> 00:11:01,452
You should get some rest
while you can.

231
00:11:01,536 --> 00:11:02,579
We'll need to be alert.

232
00:11:02,662 --> 00:11:05,790
We are here
due to my lack of caution.

233
00:11:05,874 --> 00:11:09,168
And soon, these blaggards
will sell off my sword.

234
00:11:09,627 --> 00:11:11,713
That thought fills me
with dread.

235
00:11:12,547 --> 00:11:14,507
That blade must be
more important to you

236
00:11:14,591 --> 00:11:16,134
than I'd first realized.

237
00:11:16,217 --> 00:11:18,261
You had said
it was a family heirloom, but...

238
00:11:19,596 --> 00:11:21,222
Candidly speaking,

239
00:11:21,306 --> 00:11:23,266
I was never meant
to take the throne.

240
00:11:23,349 --> 00:11:25,560
Huh? What do you mean by that?

241
00:11:26,394 --> 00:11:29,063
[RIKUYA] Please allow me
to tell you a story.

242
00:11:29,147 --> 00:11:31,983
It's about the circumstances
of my birth...

243
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:33,776
and all that transpired in Yoh.

244
00:11:35,486 --> 00:11:38,907
Since its very founding,
House Fujimiya had ruled Yoh.

245
00:11:38,990 --> 00:11:42,702
I was the fifth son born
to the 13th king's first wife.

246
00:11:42,785 --> 00:11:44,996
Rather far down
the line of succession,

247
00:11:45,079 --> 00:11:46,998
as I'm sure you'd imagine.

248
00:11:48,291 --> 00:11:50,293
And for that reason...

249
00:11:51,920 --> 00:11:53,254
Hey, Maika, Takao!

250
00:11:53,338 --> 00:11:54,797
[both exclaim]

251
00:11:55,673 --> 00:11:58,301
[RIKUYA] Unlike the controlled
life of our elder brothers,

252
00:11:58,384 --> 00:12:00,803
we could enjoy our youth,
often slipping past

253
00:12:00,887 --> 00:12:02,889
the governess
to explore the city.

254
00:12:03,848 --> 00:12:06,392
Maika and Takao
are my half-siblings,

255
00:12:06,476 --> 00:12:07,769
but we're close in age

256
00:12:07,852 --> 00:12:10,563
and regularly played
with the local children.

257
00:12:10,647 --> 00:12:12,565
We'd lose track of time

258
00:12:12,649 --> 00:12:15,568
and ourselves having fun
in the streets, until...

259
00:12:15,652 --> 00:12:17,320
Here you are!

260
00:12:17,403 --> 00:12:20,073
[RIKUYA] And without fail,
my mother came to fetch me.

261
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:22,283
You're incorrigible, child,

262
00:12:22,367 --> 00:12:25,078
leading everyone away
from the castle like that.

263
00:12:25,161 --> 00:12:26,329
[MAIKA AND TAKAO] Huh?

264
00:12:26,746 --> 00:12:29,123
-No! That was all our idea!
-No! I swear it was my idea!

265
00:12:29,207 --> 00:12:31,417
Don't lie to her.
I led everyone away.

266
00:12:31,501 --> 00:12:33,086
-[TAKAO] Come on, elder brother.
-[MAIKA] Don't say that!

267
00:12:33,169 --> 00:12:34,337
[RIKUYA] This is all on me!

268
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:37,256
-[overlapping chatter]
-[laughs]

269
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:38,800
It's time to go home!

270
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:40,927
♪

271
00:12:43,346 --> 00:12:45,473
Almost forgot. Here.

272
00:12:46,099 --> 00:12:47,100
It's a hair ornament

273
00:12:47,183 --> 00:12:48,893
made from flowers
I found in town.

274
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:51,854
I made it myself
especially for you.

275
00:12:52,438 --> 00:12:54,315
Oh, what a thoughtful boy.

276
00:12:58,945 --> 00:13:02,198
Hmm.
Looks beautiful, just like you.

277
00:13:03,199 --> 00:13:05,243
Thank you. I'll treasure it.

278
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:08,621
[RIKUYA]
I loved my life and my family,

279
00:13:08,705 --> 00:13:11,165
as well as the peace we had
in the Yoh Kingdom.

280
00:13:13,376 --> 00:13:15,378
As the three of us got older,

281
00:13:15,461 --> 00:13:16,963
they began training us

282
00:13:17,046 --> 00:13:20,341
to prepare us for supporting
our father and older brothers.

283
00:13:22,093 --> 00:13:23,594
Since Maika is so clever,

284
00:13:23,678 --> 00:13:26,014
she trained with officials
and strategists.

285
00:13:26,097 --> 00:13:28,975
The powerful Takao
trained with warriors.

286
00:13:31,227 --> 00:13:33,938
I had no clear
outstanding merits,

287
00:13:34,022 --> 00:13:36,482
but I was completely devoted
to my studies.

288
00:13:38,026 --> 00:13:39,068
[sniffs]

289
00:13:39,152 --> 00:13:40,361
Something's burning.

290
00:13:41,612 --> 00:13:42,697
[MAIKA] Elder brother!

291
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:44,282
-[woman screams]
-[RIKUYA] Uh?

292
00:13:44,615 --> 00:13:46,701
[panting]

293
00:13:48,327 --> 00:13:50,038
-[all gasp]
-[women crying]

294
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:52,081
What happened here?

295
00:13:52,165 --> 00:13:54,208
Prince Rikuya, it's an attack.

296
00:13:54,292 --> 00:13:55,835
Please, flee at-- [groans]

297
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:57,587
Get to safety.

298
00:13:57,670 --> 00:13:58,838
[squelching]

299
00:13:58,921 --> 00:14:01,883
[people screaming]

300
00:14:02,467 --> 00:14:04,927
[RIKUYA]
Father, Mother, we're coming.

301
00:14:07,305 --> 00:14:08,598
Elder brother!

302
00:14:10,767 --> 00:14:13,061
Is that you, Rikuya?

303
00:14:13,144 --> 00:14:16,397
-I'm here.
-You have to go. Now.

304
00:14:16,481 --> 00:14:18,983
Please save your strength.
You've been injured.

305
00:14:19,067 --> 00:14:19,942
[gasps]

306
00:14:20,026 --> 00:14:21,944
Father's in danger.

307
00:14:22,028 --> 00:14:24,447
You must go and protect him.
[groans]

308
00:14:25,156 --> 00:14:26,157
Brother.

309
00:14:26,657 --> 00:14:28,493
[crying]

310
00:14:28,576 --> 00:14:29,869
Brother, no!

311
00:14:30,370 --> 00:14:32,038
You can't die!

312
00:14:33,456 --> 00:14:34,582
[RIKUYA] Why?

313
00:14:35,124 --> 00:14:37,460
Why did they have to be
slaughtered like that?

314
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:39,545
Father, are you in here?

315
00:14:39,629 --> 00:14:41,214
[Rikuya's Father groaning]

316
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:43,591
[gasps]

317
00:14:46,385 --> 00:14:49,222
Rikuya. [groaning]

318
00:14:50,181 --> 00:14:51,307
[RIKUYA] Father!

319
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:53,976
I was betrayed
by my closest retainers.

320
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:55,728
They want to take the throne.

321
00:14:55,812 --> 00:14:57,438
An uprising?

322
00:14:57,522 --> 00:15:00,233
Mother... has someone
taken her to safety?

323
00:15:00,316 --> 00:15:03,694
No. That traitorous bunch
has taken her.

324
00:15:06,239 --> 00:15:07,281
Rikuya...

325
00:15:07,824 --> 00:15:09,283
take this sword and go.

326
00:15:10,159 --> 00:15:12,662
[RIKUYA] But Father,
this belongs to the king.

327
00:15:12,745 --> 00:15:13,746
That's right.

328
00:15:15,456 --> 00:15:17,625
You must become
the next King of Yoh!

329
00:15:17,708 --> 00:15:19,502
That sword is crucial

330
00:15:19,585 --> 00:15:22,255
if you are to reclaim
our family's historic legacy!

331
00:15:22,338 --> 00:15:23,881
But I can't be the king!

332
00:15:23,965 --> 00:15:25,508
There has to be some other--

333
00:15:25,591 --> 00:15:27,385
[rebels shouting]

334
00:15:27,468 --> 00:15:29,846
You can escape through here,
young master.

335
00:15:31,597 --> 00:15:32,807
[gasping]

336
00:15:35,351 --> 00:15:37,562
[RIKUYA'S FATHER]
We'll hold them off. Now go!

337
00:15:39,313 --> 00:15:41,566
Our future is in your hands.

338
00:15:41,649 --> 00:15:43,317
[breathes shakily]

339
00:15:46,487 --> 00:15:47,822
[RIKUYA]
The retainers' rebellion

340
00:15:47,905 --> 00:15:50,283
stripped House Fujimiya
of the kingship.

341
00:15:51,033 --> 00:15:54,203
Only Maika, Takao,
and I escaped their wrath.

342
00:15:54,287 --> 00:15:55,705
♪

343
00:15:56,789 --> 00:15:59,959
[running footsteps]

344
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:01,502
[panting]

345
00:16:02,295 --> 00:16:04,463
Elder brother, listen to me.

346
00:16:04,547 --> 00:16:06,132
We have to leave now.

347
00:16:06,215 --> 00:16:09,427
Those vile traitors
have already taken full control.

348
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:10,803
And what of Mother?

349
00:16:11,345 --> 00:16:14,265
I'm afraid the usurper's
forced her to become his bride.

350
00:16:14,974 --> 00:16:18,269
But she's really his hostage.
He's locked her away!

351
00:16:18,352 --> 00:16:20,897
[Rikuya grunting]

352
00:16:22,732 --> 00:16:23,858
[RIKUYA] I swear...
[clenching fists]

353
00:16:23,941 --> 00:16:24,901
[BOTH] Uh?

354
00:16:25,526 --> 00:16:28,112
[RIKUYA] We will return
and set her free!

355
00:16:29,113 --> 00:16:30,907
Or die trying!

356
00:16:34,911 --> 00:16:37,705
[RIKUYA] As for the rest,
it's just as I've told you.

357
00:16:38,372 --> 00:16:40,583
We've been traveling
between kingdoms

358
00:16:40,666 --> 00:16:42,043
hoping to find some help.

359
00:16:42,126 --> 00:16:43,461
[Ars gasps softly]

360
00:16:44,086 --> 00:16:45,129
[RIKUYA] Truthfully,

361
00:16:45,796 --> 00:16:48,090
I possess neither
the wisdom of Maika

362
00:16:48,174 --> 00:16:50,468
nor the natural strength
of Takao.

363
00:16:50,551 --> 00:16:53,262
Alas, as living heir
to the throne,

364
00:16:53,346 --> 00:16:55,056
I must reclaim my kingdom.

365
00:16:55,139 --> 00:16:56,849
As a lord myself,

366
00:16:56,933 --> 00:16:59,060
I can understand
how you're feeling inside.

367
00:17:00,603 --> 00:17:01,896
Tell me this...

368
00:17:02,813 --> 00:17:05,399
have you ever given much thought
to your bloodline?

369
00:17:06,567 --> 00:17:08,653
Those of us born
to noble families

370
00:17:08,736 --> 00:17:10,821
are destined
to inherit authority.

371
00:17:10,905 --> 00:17:13,074
But why, exactly?

372
00:17:13,908 --> 00:17:16,452
Simply because royal blood
runs through our veins?

373
00:17:19,163 --> 00:17:22,041
I don't believe that
such things have any meaning.

374
00:17:22,124 --> 00:17:23,376
At the very least,

375
00:17:23,459 --> 00:17:25,878
none that can be seen
with the naked eye.

376
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:28,631
In that regard,

377
00:17:28,714 --> 00:17:31,717
I am naught but a talentless
and ignorant youth.

378
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:36,180
Can someone like me,
a complete mediocrity...

379
00:17:36,889 --> 00:17:40,518
Is it even possible for me
to bear the weight of a kingdom?

380
00:17:40,601 --> 00:17:41,686
[Ars gasps softly]

381
00:17:42,645 --> 00:17:45,022
[RIKUYA]
So that sword is all I have.

382
00:17:45,815 --> 00:17:48,234
The only way
to prove my claim to the throne

383
00:17:48,317 --> 00:17:51,195
is the sword with the power
to best a legendary beast,

384
00:17:51,279 --> 00:17:52,989
the Dragonslayer Blade!

385
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:57,493
Only when I hold that sword
do I rise above this mediocrity.

386
00:17:59,495 --> 00:18:00,997
Now it's gone,

387
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:04,208
and nothing else that I possess
could prove that I am king.

388
00:18:05,084 --> 00:18:07,920
Rikuya, I think you're wrong
about all of that.

389
00:18:08,004 --> 00:18:09,005
[gasps softly]

390
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:10,464
[gate opens]

391
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:13,426
[BANDIT] Uh, boss,
what are you doing down here?

392
00:18:13,509 --> 00:18:15,845
[VIGO]
Give me the kid, the Malkan,

393
00:18:15,928 --> 00:18:17,388
and the guy with the long hair.

394
00:18:17,471 --> 00:18:20,641
[chuckles]
We're gonna have some fun.

395
00:18:20,725 --> 00:18:22,893
[hisses]

396
00:18:29,567 --> 00:18:33,195
[VIGO] You see, the thing is,
I hate liars.

397
00:18:33,279 --> 00:18:35,531
I've always been
a straight-shooter,

398
00:18:35,614 --> 00:18:39,702
but some people just can't seem
to keep themselves honest.

399
00:18:40,411 --> 00:18:44,790
I have no choice but to punish
those who refuse to be truthful.

400
00:18:46,709 --> 00:18:49,086
-[ARS] I see now.
-This sword,

401
00:18:49,170 --> 00:18:51,047
it really is something special,
huh?

402
00:18:51,714 --> 00:18:53,841
My men might have
bought your story.

403
00:18:53,924 --> 00:18:55,176
But I gotta wonder...

404
00:18:55,468 --> 00:18:58,638
What's a traveler like you
doing with such a fine blade?

405
00:18:59,639 --> 00:19:02,433
That sword
is an old family heirloom.

406
00:19:02,516 --> 00:19:04,935
It was passed down
to me by my father.

407
00:19:05,019 --> 00:19:06,020
[grunts]

408
00:19:07,188 --> 00:19:08,356
[groans]

409
00:19:08,773 --> 00:19:10,858
[VIGO] There's no way in hell
you're a simple traveler.

410
00:19:10,941 --> 00:19:13,402
I swear to God,
he's telling you the truth.

411
00:19:13,861 --> 00:19:14,904
[VIGO] Huh?

412
00:19:15,446 --> 00:19:17,406
[ARS]
Why are you doing all of this?

413
00:19:17,490 --> 00:19:19,575
You were a soldier
in the Seitz army, weren't you?

414
00:19:19,659 --> 00:19:23,329
-[Rietz gasps]
-Oh, figured that out, huh?

415
00:19:23,412 --> 00:19:25,331
You claim that you're
from a merchant family,

416
00:19:25,414 --> 00:19:26,874
but I know the truth.

417
00:19:26,957 --> 00:19:28,584
I recognize your face

418
00:19:28,668 --> 00:19:30,711
from seeing you
on the battlefield, kid.

419
00:19:30,795 --> 00:19:33,339
We've got Ars Louvent,
in the flesh.

420
00:19:33,422 --> 00:19:35,925
And Rietz Muses,
"the Reaper of Lamberg."

421
00:19:36,008 --> 00:19:39,345
Matter of fact,
you took my damn eye

422
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:41,305
during the fight
at the Coumeire River.

423
00:19:41,389 --> 00:19:44,100
So you and I
got a little bit of history.

424
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:45,643
After losing,

425
00:19:45,976 --> 00:19:48,270
my men and I decided
to become bandits instead.

426
00:19:48,354 --> 00:19:50,106
Best decision of my life.

427
00:19:50,189 --> 00:19:52,983
The pay is much better
than what they give to soldiers.

428
00:19:53,067 --> 00:19:54,652
But the best thing about it...

429
00:19:55,361 --> 00:19:57,029
I hold the power
of life and death

430
00:19:57,113 --> 00:19:58,489
over those who beat Borotz.

431
00:19:58,572 --> 00:20:00,616
But I won't fail like he did.

432
00:20:01,367 --> 00:20:04,703
Lay one finger on Lord Ars
and you'll be dead

433
00:20:04,787 --> 00:20:07,665
before your body
even crashes to the ground.

434
00:20:08,082 --> 00:20:09,333
[chuckles]

435
00:20:09,417 --> 00:20:11,669
You were that cocky
on the battlefield too.

436
00:20:12,420 --> 00:20:14,130
Look, I'm not gonna kill you.

437
00:20:14,213 --> 00:20:16,966
No one's gonna pay me squat
for a dead Malkan.

438
00:20:17,049 --> 00:20:18,884
But now I've got the man
who took my eye

439
00:20:18,968 --> 00:20:21,178
and lied to my face
on his knees before me.

440
00:20:21,262 --> 00:20:23,722
-It's time for some payback.
-Oh, no! Rietz!

441
00:20:23,806 --> 00:20:26,517
[laughs] Ah, come on.

442
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:28,727
Where'd all that attitude go,
huh?

443
00:20:28,811 --> 00:20:30,729
[grunting]

444
00:20:31,939 --> 00:20:34,233
Well, look at that.
Aren't you a quiet one?

445
00:20:35,276 --> 00:20:36,944
I guess an old slave like you

446
00:20:37,027 --> 00:20:38,863
must have gotten
used to being whipped.

447
00:20:39,321 --> 00:20:40,364
[grunts]

448
00:20:40,781 --> 00:20:42,908
[laughing]

449
00:20:42,992 --> 00:20:44,118
-[ARS] Stop this!
-Huh?

450
00:20:45,077 --> 00:20:46,996
[ARS]
Yes, I lied about who I am,

451
00:20:47,079 --> 00:20:48,998
but if you want
to punish someone,

452
00:20:49,081 --> 00:20:51,625
as his master,
you should punish me.

453
00:20:51,709 --> 00:20:53,544
No, Lord Ars, please don't.

454
00:20:53,627 --> 00:20:55,755
This kid has got
some real stones on him.

455
00:20:57,673 --> 00:20:59,216
[gasps, coughs]

456
00:20:59,300 --> 00:21:02,011
-[RIETZ] Lord Ars!
-Oh! Not so tough now!

457
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:04,972
Is it your first time
with a whip, boy? [laughs]

458
00:21:05,055 --> 00:21:07,308
-[whipping]
-[RIETZ] Stop it!

459
00:21:07,808 --> 00:21:09,018
[VIGO] Say whatever you want

460
00:21:09,101 --> 00:21:11,312
until the whip starts asking
the questions,

461
00:21:11,395 --> 00:21:14,023
then you got no choice
but to be honest.

462
00:21:15,191 --> 00:21:16,859
You wanna say...

463
00:21:17,568 --> 00:21:20,738
"Hit my slave
instead of me, sir." That right?

464
00:21:21,363 --> 00:21:23,407
That would be for the best.
I can take it--

465
00:21:23,491 --> 00:21:24,825
[ARS] No! Hit me!

466
00:21:24,909 --> 00:21:26,035
[gasps]

467
00:21:28,829 --> 00:21:30,664
Why would you want to spare him?

468
00:21:31,373 --> 00:21:35,669
[ARS] Because without Rietz,
I am nothing.

469
00:21:36,253 --> 00:21:38,130
The only thing
that makes me a lord

470
00:21:38,214 --> 00:21:40,424
is all the people
who believe in me.

471
00:21:40,508 --> 00:21:41,592
So, no.

472
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:45,596
I cannot allow you
to harm my retainers!

473
00:21:45,679 --> 00:21:46,847
[cries]

474
00:21:47,139 --> 00:21:48,432
[grunts]

475
00:21:48,516 --> 00:21:49,683
♪

476
00:21:55,022 --> 00:21:58,359
[♪ closing theme song playing]

477
00:23:26,238 --> 00:23:28,157
[ZAHT] Way to use
your head back there, Captain.

478
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:29,950
[JOE] Yeah, I'm pretty badass.

479
00:23:30,034 --> 00:23:31,410
[ZAHT]
You don't do sarcasm, huh?

480
00:23:31,493 --> 00:23:33,412
[JOE] What's that?
Some kind of weird food?

481
00:23:33,495 --> 00:23:35,748
[Zaht sighs] When he said
you need schooling,

482
00:23:35,831 --> 00:23:36,957
he was right.

483
00:23:37,041 --> 00:23:39,543
Next time, "What a King Needs."

